### Disable deployment for specific branch

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Prevent automated deployments on a specific branch like 'dev'. Use vercel.json for static configuration or vercel.ts for programmatic configuration.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "git": {
    "deploymentEnabled": {
      "dev": false
    }
  }
}
```

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  git: {
    deploymentEnabled: {
      dev: false,
    },
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Disable deployments for branches matching pattern

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Use minimatch syntax to prevent deployments for multiple branches matching a pattern, such as all branches starting with 'internal-'.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "git": {
    "deploymentEnabled": {
      "internal-*": false
    }
  }
}
```

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  git: {
    deploymentEnabled: {
      'internal-*': false,
    },
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Disable Vercel Toolbar for a specific branch

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-toolbar/managing-toolbar

Use this environment variable to disable the Vercel Toolbar for a specific preview branch. Set its value to '0'.

```txt
VERCEL_PREVIEW_FEEDBACK_ENABLED=0
```

--------------------------------

### Update Environment Variable for Specific Environment and Git Branch (Vercel CLI)

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/cli/env

Use this command to update an existing environment variable's value for a specific environment and Git branch.

```bash
vercel env update [name] [environment] [gitbranch]
```

--------------------------------

### Configure github.enabled in vercel.json

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Disable auto-deployments for your project using the deprecated github.enabled property in vercel.json. This property has been superseded by the git.deploymentEnabled setting.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "github": {
    "enabled": false
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Listing Environment Variables for a Specific Environment and Git Branch

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/cli/env

Lists environment variables filtered by a specified deployment environment and a particular Git branch.

```bash
vercel env ls [environment] [gitbranch]
```

--------------------------------

### Disable all automatic deployments

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Turn off automatic deployments for all branches by setting deploymentEnabled to false.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "git": {
    "deploymentEnabled": false
  }
}
```

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  git: {
    deploymentEnabled: false,
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Inspecting a specific Vercel deployment

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/rollback-production-deployment

Retrieve detailed information about a specific deployment, such as its Git commit SHA, branch, and build time, for further investigation.

```bash
vercel inspect <bad-deployment-url>
```

--------------------------------

### Configure github.enabled in vercel.ts

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Disable auto-deployments for your project using the deprecated github.enabled property in vercel.ts. This property has been superseded by the git.deploymentEnabled setting.

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  github: {
    enabled: false,
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Adding an Environment Variable to a Specific Git Branch

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/cli/env

Adds a new environment variable with the specified name, scoped to a particular deployment environment and Git branch.

```bash
vercel env add [name] [environment] [gitbranch]
```

--------------------------------

### Specify Package Manager in vercel.json

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/package-managers

Use the `installCommand` property in your project's `vercel.json` file to specify a package manager for a specific deployment.

```json
{  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",  "installCommand": "pnpm install"}
```

--------------------------------

### Add branch-specific preview variable

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/environment-variables/manage-across-environments

Set environment variables that only apply to preview deployments from a specific Git branch. Useful for testing against different databases or API endpoints on feature branches.

```bash
vercel env add DATABASE_URL preview feature-branch
```

--------------------------------

### Remove all deployments for a project with vercel remove

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/cli/remove

Remove all deployments for a Vercel Project by providing the project name. Removes the entire project unless --safe flag is used.

```bash
vercel remove [project-name]
```

--------------------------------

### Create a New Deployment with Vercel SDK

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/rest-api/sdk/deployments/create-a-new-deployment

Use this snippet to initiate a new deployment, specifying project settings, Git metadata, and files. It supports forcing a new deployment and skipping auto-detection confirmation.

```javascript
import { Vercel } from "@vercel/sdk";

const vercel = new Vercel({
  bearerToken: "<YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN_HERE>",
});

async function run() {
  const result = await vercel.deployments.createDeployment({
    forceNew: "1",
    skipAutoDetectionConfirmation: "1",
    teamId: "REDACTED",
    slug: "my-team-url-slug",
    requestBody: {
      customEnvironmentSlugOrId: "staging",
      deploymentId: "REDACTED",
      files: [
        {
          file: "folder/file.js",
        }
      ],
      gitMetadata: {
        remoteUrl: "https://github.com/vercel/next.js",
        commitAuthorName: "kyliau",
        commitAuthorEmail: "kyliau@example.com",
        commitMessage: "add method to measure Interaction to Next Paint (INP) (#36490)",
        commitRef: "main",
        commitSha: "dc36199b2234c6586ebe05ec94078a895c707e29",
        dirty: true,
        ci: true,
        ciType: "github-actions",
        ciGitProviderUsername: "rauchg",
        ciGitRepoVisibility: "private"
      },
      gitSource: {
        org: "vercel",
        ref: "main",
        repo: "next.js",
        sha: "REDACTED",
        type: "github"
      },
      meta: {
        "foo": "bar"
      },
      name: "my-instant-deployment",
      project: "my-deployment-project",
      projectSettings: {
        buildCommand: "next build",
        installCommand: "pnpm install"
      },
      target: "production"
    }
  });

  console.log(result);
}

run();
```

